hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20964","Affan narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, a shaykh from Banu Salit informed me, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, speaking to him about captives taken for us in the Jahiliyyah, and he was narrating to the people with a circle surrounding him, and he was sitting with a thick Qitri waist-wrapper upon him. The first thing I heard from him saying, while saying with his hand thus, and al-Mubarak pointed with his index finger: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here, piety is here, meaning in the heart."
"20965","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from al-Hasan, a man from Banu Salit narrated to me, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in a crowd of people, and I heard him say: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here. Hammad said: And he said with his hand to his chest. And no two love one another for Allah, mighty and majestic, but nothing separates them except an act one of them commits, and the innovator is evil, and the innovator is evil, and the innovator is evil."
